{
    "title": "onX Backcountry Trail Maps GPS",
    "description": "\u25b6The Ultimate GPS Map App for Your Outdoor Pursuits\r\nonX Backcountry lets you easily find and navigate trails\u2014whether you\u2019re seeking new backcountry skiing lines, climbing routes, or hiking trails and mountain bike trails. Plan your hiking trails and mountain bikes trails with the best trail maps and trustworthy info, and navigate confidently with offline trail maps and GPS tracking.\r\n\r\n\u25b6Discover New Adventures\r\nWhether navigating mountain bike trails, hiking trails, skiing routes, or a backpacking trip, we\u2019ve got you covered with over 650k miles of trails.\r\n\r\n\u25b6Prep Better With Powerful Trail Maps Tools\r\nWe adventure in three dimensions, and your trail maps should reflect that. With a 3D map, you can visualize mountain bike trails, scout skiing lines, and plan for hazards before you hit the trail. See recent conditions with weather forecasts, reports from other trail users, and get snow info from SNOTEL stations and regional avalanche forecasts to plan your skiing adventure. Map out custom hiking trails and mountain bike trails with snap-to-trail functionality, and use Waypoints, Slope Angle, Slope Aspect, Trail Slope, and Wildfire Layers for detailed hike planning.\r\n\r\n\u25b6Hike & Navigate Without Cell Coverage\r\nSave Offline Trail Maps to bring your custom maps when you're outside cell coverage. With the onX Backcountry App, turn your phone into a handheld GPS device using your phone's internal GPS. Navigate hiking trails & mountain biking trails offline by following the blue dot to always know how to get home. Leave a breadcrumb trail with Tracker to see where you\u2019ve been and measure your key trip stats.\r\n\r\n\u25b6The Best Maps\r\nWith map data sourced from USFS, BLM, and NPS, our color-coded base maps help you easily find what you\u2019re looking for. Scout the landscape and visualize terrain by viewing your trail maps in 3D, topo, satellite imagery, or a hybrid.\r\n\r\n\u25b6PREMIUM AND ELITE FEATURES:\r\n650,000+ miles of running trails, hiking trails, backpacking trails, and mountain bike trails\r\n4,000+ backcountry skiing lines with guidebook descriptions\r\n300,000+ rock climbing routes with approach trails\r\nSnap-to-trail route builder to plan trips and see distance and elevation gain in seconds\r\nSave unlimited Offline Trail Maps for offline trail maps navigation without cell service\r\nGPS tracking to know where you came from, how to get back, and share your adventure\r\nLocalized weather conditions and 7-day weather forecasts\r\n24K topographic maps and 3D maps for the entire U.S.\r\n985 million acres of Public Land across the U.S.\r\n550,000 Recreation Icons for points of interest, including trailheads, backcountry cabins and lookouts, campgrounds & dispersed camping land\r\nAvalanche forecasts for the U.S. & Canada\r\nRecent snowfall information & historic trends via SNOTEL data\r\nThe best GPS trail maps to navigate on your backcountry hiking trails, mountain bike trails, climbing, and skiing trails\r\nPrivate Land Layer-ELITE ONLY: Private property maps & land boundaries, land ownership info, and acreage\r\nRecent Imagery-ELITE ONLY: Detailed satellite imagery from the past two weeks\r\n\r\n\u25b6Free Trial\r\nWhile the onX Backcountry App and many features are free, you\u2019ll start a free Premium or Elite trial when you install the App. This lets you try many of our best features, like 3D trail maps, unlimited offline downloads, trail info, and guidebook backcountry skiing lines. After the first seven days, you\u2019ll still have access to beautiful topo and satellite maps, GPS tracking, weather, and more.\r\n\r\n\u25b6Feedback\r\nIf you have any trouble or have an idea on what you\u2019d like to see next, contact us at support@onxmaps.com. \r\n\r\n\u25b6 Your Four Season Adventure App\r\nWhether you\u2019re into hiking trails, mountain bike trails, skiing, or backpacking trips, our app has the features you need to plan, navigate, and share your adventures. Download and start your next hiking, skiing, or mountain biking journey with onX Backcountry. From hiking trails, skiing, to enjoyable mountain bike trails, onX Backcountry has everything you need.",
    "descriptionHTML": "\u25b6The Ultimate GPS Map App for Your Outdoor Pursuits<br>onX Backcountry lets you easily find and navigate trails\u2014whether you\u2019re seeking new backcountry skiing lines, climbing routes, or hiking trails and mountain bike trails. Plan your hiking trails and mountain bikes trails with the best trail maps and trustworthy info, and navigate confidently with offline trail maps and GPS tracking.<br><br>\u25b6Discover New Adventures<br>Whether navigating mountain bike trails, hiking trails, skiing routes, or a backpacking trip, we\u2019ve got you covered with over 650k miles of trails.<br><br>\u25b6Prep Better With Powerful Trail Maps Tools<br>We adventure in three dimensions, and your trail maps should reflect that. With a 3D map, you can visualize mountain bike trails, scout skiing lines, and plan for hazards before you hit the trail. See recent conditions with weather forecasts, reports from other trail users, and get snow info from SNOTEL stations and regional avalanche forecasts to plan your skiing adventure. Map out custom hiking trails and mountain bike trails with snap-to-trail functionality, and use Waypoints, Slope Angle, Slope Aspect, Trail Slope, and Wildfire Layers for detailed hike planning.<br><br>\u25b6Hike &amp; Navigate Without Cell Coverage<br>Save Offline Trail Maps to bring your custom maps when you&#39;re outside cell coverage. With the onX Backcountry App, turn your phone into a handheld GPS device using your phone&#39;s internal GPS. Navigate hiking trails &amp; mountain biking trails offline by following the blue dot to always know how to get home. Leave a breadcrumb trail with Tracker to see where you\u2019ve been and measure your key trip stats.<br><br>\u25b6The Best Maps<br>With map data sourced from USFS, BLM, and NPS, our color-coded base maps help you easily find what you\u2019re looking for. Scout the landscape and visualize terrain by viewing your trail maps in 3D, topo, satellite imagery, or a hybrid.<br>